WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.934 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Do you miss it?

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:03.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you desperately miss no
having been

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.070 size:88% position:44% line:92%
on stage this last year?

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:07.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I've been doing TV
for all of these years.

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:09.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
I miss the stage,
that's for sure,

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:11.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I've been doing
"Good Fight now for 12 years

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:14.180
and I just started doing
"The Gilded Age" for HBO.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I've been lucky
because if you work on film,

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.152 size:78% position:39%
we've somehow managed
to go back to work.

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:23.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
We wear masks, and, you know
when they say action,

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:25.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
we take the mask off
and we act and everybody

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:28.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
is all covered up,
and then when they say cut

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
we have to put the masks
back on,

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:31.398 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
but we've managed.

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:35.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's people who work on stages
that haven't had --

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:35.835 size:75% position:38% line:92%
really had it rough.

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:40.607
But that said, a lot of thes
great theater actors have foun

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:45.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
a place working in New York --
in New York TV shows.

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:49.115
-Now, "Gilded Age," I believe,
Cynthia Nixon is in. Correct

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:50.383 line:92%
-Yes, she plays my sister.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:53.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you have been on Broadway
together in the past.

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:57.657
-She played my daughter
in "The Real Thing back in 1984.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:01:01.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was a student at Barnard
and I played her mother.

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:02.996 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Now she's my sister.

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:03.997 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm like, "Okay."

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:06.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
That's good.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
That means you're doing doin
great, by the way.

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:10.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-If your daughter is aged

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
into your sister,
you're doing great.

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:14.607
It's when it's the other way
around, you're like "Oh, no.

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:16.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I agree.
-And then also, you know,

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:19.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
you mentioned "The Good Figh
is a show, obviously,

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:20.980 line:92%
that multiple Broadway people...

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God.
It's a revolving door.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:25.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have -- now, this episode
we have Stephen Lang

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:28.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Mandy Patinkin
and Jane Curtin

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:29.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
is playing a judge.
It's a hoot.

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:33.493
We have the most wonderful
character actors come on,

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:34.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they are all
theater trained,

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
so it's like a repertory
company.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:38.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And Audrey -- you mentioned
Audra,

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:43.570 size:78% position:39%
and you presented her
with her first Tony.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.271 line:92%
-Yes, the young Audra McDonald

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:49.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
now my colleague
on "The Good Fight." Yeah

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:51.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you remember who gave yo
your first Tony?

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:54.047 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Yes, and my second.

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:56.216 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Um, my sec...

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:57.350 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:00.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can't remember who gave m
my 15th, but...

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:04.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The first two.
You never forget the first two

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:04.591 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
-John Lithgow.
-Oh, what a perfect person

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:08.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it was great.
Yeah.

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:10.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You must have felt lucky
the second time

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.999 line:92%
Lithgow was handing them out

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:13.466 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:16.936
It's always amazing to win
a Tony award, but the first time

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:18.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
was just like it was
Mike Nickels

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:20.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Tom Stoppard
wrote this play

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:22.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Jeremy Irons
and Glenn Close,

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.677 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and we all won Tonys.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:25.278 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was just...

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:27.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you remember that nigh
afterwards?

00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:31.251
Was it just sort of night
you dream of the first tim

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:33.353 line:92%
you win an award like that

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:34.954 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I can't --

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:39.259
Julie Andrews and Robert Preston
hosted the event.

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:42.595 size:75% position:38%
I mean, two legends,
and I came off stage

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:45.865
just having won the Tony,
and they grab it from you

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:47.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they have to put
your name on it.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:49.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they grab it from me.
-I was so worried

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.171 line:92%
because there's only one Tony.

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:51.871 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Just to speak to why

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.107 size:88% position:44% line:92%
we need the actors fund.

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:56.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's only -- Do you kno
there's one Tony?

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:57.911 line:92%
-And it just revolves, yeah.

00:02:57.911 --> 00:03:01.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
Anyway, I remember leaning
against a wall

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:03.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it's like,
you go into --

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:04.584 line:92%
it's an out of body experience

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:08.054
The adrenaline rush is so
strong, and this woman

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:11.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
kind went past me
and went, "Congratulations."

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:16.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was in black velvet
and diamonds, and it was like,

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:17.263 size:78% position:39% line:92%
it was Julie Andrews.

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:20.767
She was about to, you know
continue her hostess duties,

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:22.135 size:88% position:44% line:92%
but it was such a night.

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:24.704 size:78% position:39%
It was such -- yeah,
I remember the party.

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:25.405 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I remember everything.

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:28.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And we, you know, we have
talked before

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:30.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the fact that
the great thing about the Tony

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:34.847
is I think you were telling me
you grew up in Buffalo, right?

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and I used to watch
the Tonys.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:38.885
-Yeah.
-And I watched -- the first time

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:42.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
I watched the Tonys,
Lauren Bacall won

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:46.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
for "Applause,"
then all those years later

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:48.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got to honor her
at the Kennedy Center

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:49.562 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and stand center stage.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:53.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was honored with Bob Dylan
I was remember Bob --

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
Bob and Loren sitting next
to each other,

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:58.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was singing
"Welcome To The Theatre"

00:03:58.705 --> 00:04:01.140 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to Lauren Bacall.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.543
Just there's nothing more
terrifying then looking up

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:09.616
and seeing Bob Dylan watchin
you sing and Lauren Bacall

00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:14.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. So, do the you still --
do you still get nervous?

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:14.821 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, I do.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you think nerves
are good as a performer?

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:17.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
When people ask me
about butterflies,

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:21.060
I do think for certain thing
butterflies are a very helpful

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:24.397 line:92%
reminder that it's time focus.

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:26.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I would worry
if I weren't nervous.

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:30.103
The trick is that you don't want
your fear to choke you.

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:31.204 line:92%
You must know as a performer

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:35.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
The worst thing that can happe
is you clutch

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:37.310 line:92%
and then you can't think.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:39.812
You have to kind of make friends
with your fear,

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:43.850 size:75% position:38%
and that's something
that comes with age.

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:45.351 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:46.152 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:48.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
They give it to you
with your second Tony.

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:50.690 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.091 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-But yeah, I'm always.

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:56.129 size:88% position:44%
I'm nervous by they say
action when I'm filming.

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:57.864 line:92%
I think it's a good thing.

00:04:57.864 --> 00:04:59.599 line:92%
Adrenaline helps focus the mind.

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:02.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
Too much of it chokes you,
but just enough

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:04.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
gives you that --
that lovely buzz.

00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:06.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, thank you so much
for being here.

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:07.040 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, thank you.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.908 size:88% position:44%
Thank you for letting me
talk about the auction.

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:11.177 size:81% position:41%
It would mean so much
to raise lots of money

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:14.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
for all my theater pals
and all the people

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:17.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the performer arts.
-It's weird you e-mailed Loren

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:19.986 line:92%
for Tina's number and not mine

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:22.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
Christine Baranski, everyone
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.355 --> 00:05:26.225
The Stage &amp; Screen auction
hosted by Doyle auctioneer

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:28.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
and appraises will begin
at 10:00 A.M.

00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:29.562 line:92%
on Wednesday April, 28th.

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:33.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll be right back
